Z||000022||WhiteFieroBlur||10-29-2001||03:43 PM||||What I wanna know is, how in the world do you get the stock shift nob off. I one day kept pulling and pulling and slid up a lil and stopped. I was too afraid I was gonna break something. is there some trick to get these off?||||reg||1
Z||000023||WhiteFieroBlur||10-29-2001||03:44 PM||||my bad I have the 87 GT 5 speed manual shifter||||reg||1
Z||000024||85ZainoGT||10-29-2001||03:44 PM||||you screw it off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000025||MinnGreenGT||10-29-2001||03:47 PM||||Yes, there is a specific way to remove the stock auto-shifter handle.  It's usually easiest to pull the shifter into 1st or 2nd gear (the farther back the handle the easier).  Then on the front side of the "T" there is a small rectangular cut in the handle & leather.  There is a medium sized "c-clip" (Looks like a big staple) that can be easily removed with a needlenose or regular pliers.  Once you remove the clip, it'll just slide right off!<P>The shift knobs from JCW are mounted with 3 set-screws that just tighten onto the shaft, and are then covered with another threaded cap.  Simple install- takes 5-10 minutes at the longest.  I have had to re-tighten my handle twice now... I guess the pointed tips of the set screws probably wear a little.<P>[EDIT] Well-damn.  I finally got the whole thing typed out and it's a stick!  Oh well... now if anyone else doesn't know- this is for you! [/EDIT]<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||WhiteFieroBlur||10-30-2001||01:50 AM||||Well Green thanx for the info but as you noticed I have a stick shift fiero not an automatic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, so am I to asume I just screw it off like some screw or something and not pull it off with all my might?||||reg||1
Z||000027||Monkeyman||10-30-2001||04:35 AM||||WhiteFieroBlur--Just unscrew the manual shifter knob.||||reg||1
